    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d804">

                <pb facs="0821" n="815" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg815"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/1145</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Greek Minister (Diamantopoulos) to the Chief of the Division of Near Eastern
                        Affairs (Murray)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-08">January 8,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Murray</hi>: From certain Greek quarters
                    anxious to show loyalty and devotion to the United States in their war effort,
                    and their willingness to make any sacrifice for the common cause, I have been
                    asked to inquire if the formations of Greek volunteer units will be agreeable to
                    the United States Military Authorities.</p>
                <pb facs="0822" n="816" xml:id="pg816"/>
                <p>I should be much obliged, my dear Mr. Murray, if you kindly informed me
                    accordingly.</p>
                <p>With my kind personal regards,</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Diamantopoulos</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
